!! Capturing a fleeting note

Click an area pill (e.g. ''llm'') in the topbar, then ''+ Note''. Type ''typescript-tips'' and submit. A new tiddler appears at `knowledge/llm/typescript-tips` (or `knowledge/inbox/typescript-tips` if no area was active) with body:

```
\context knowledge

```

…and `kn.tier=fleeting`.

!! Descendant linking from a deep parent

In a note titled `knowledge/llm/vendor/deepseek/model/v4`, write:

```
See the engineering deep-dive at [[yt/AIsearch/engineeringDSV4]].
```

The link resolves to `knowledge/llm/vendor/deepseek/model/v4/yt/AIsearch/engineeringDSV4` — namespace's ''self-prefix'' stage tries `<sourceTitle>/<ref>` automatically (this plugin enables that flag by default; toggle it off in ControlPanel under Namespace settings if you want strict resolution).

The opposite direction (child → parent) still works via walk-up: from the deep note above, `[[v4]]` finds the parent `…/model/v4` because walk-up climbs ancestor segments.

!! Linking by short ref

In a note titled `knowledge/topics/programming/typescript/Foo`, write:

```
\context knowledge

See also [[Bar]] for details, or [[topics/python/Snake]] for the cousin language.
```

The namespace walk-up resolves `[[Bar]]` against the source's path: tries `knowledge/topics/programming/typescript/Bar`, then `knowledge/topics/programming/Bar`, then `knowledge/topics/Bar`, etc. The relative path `topics/python/Snake` walks up too: `…/typescript/topics/python/Snake` (no), `…/programming/topics/python/Snake` (no), `…/topics/python/Snake` (yes, if it exists).

!! Cross-app linking

In an orga app meeting note (e.g. `orga/meetings/2026-04-30/notes`), write:

```
Discussion ref: [[kn/topics/programming/typescript/Foo]]
```

The starter mount `kn → knowledge` rewrites the prefix, and the link resolves to `knowledge/topics/programming/typescript/Foo`.

!! Topic index page

Create a tiddler `knowledge/topics/typescript/index` summarising the topic. From any note in that tree (or anywhere with the right context), write `[[knowledge/topics/typescript/_index]]` — the `_index` pseudo expands to `index` (or `README`) at that prefix.

!! Filtering the mindmap

Click ''🌳 Evergreen'' in the chip strip above the mindmap. The tree prunes to evergreen-tier notes ''plus their ancestors'' (so the path stays visible). Click again to deselect. Add ''📚 Source'' (type chip) to intersect: the canvas now shows only evergreen sources and the area roots leading to them. Click chips again to clear.

!! Changing a note's type

In the mindmap preview pane (right edge), click the type pill at the top of the body (e.g. ''💡 Idea''). A popup opens with all 15 types grouped Core / Entity / Structural. Pick a new one — the `kn.type` field is updated in place, and the type chip filter above the mindmap will treat the note accordingly on the next chip click.

!! Capture a source note (TZK-style)

Click ''+ Note'', set ''Type'' to ''Source''. Extra fields appear:

* ''Caption'' — display label (e.g. "Atomic Habits").
* ''Author'' — e.g. "James Clear".
* ''Medium'' — article / book / youtube / podcast / blog.
* ''URL'' — full link (any form).
* ''Published'' — toggle between ''Year'' (number input) and ''Date'' (full date picker).
* ''Consume status'' — created / partial / consumed / reconsumed.
* ''Consume date'' — date picker.

After Create, the new note's fields are stamped. Note: as of 0.1.20 the structured "source card" render (YouTube embed + definition list) is temporarily unwired — the previous note-view that hosted `forms/render-source` was retired with the section model. Re-integration via a custom `mm.preview-body-template` is on the follow-up list; in the meantime, the source fields are visible in the field bar of the popup editor.

